MODEL WATCH #58 — Wednesday, September 23, 2026

1. OPENROUTER ANNOUNCES VOLUME PRICING ON DEEPSEEK-V4 PRO, ROUGHLY 30% LOWER, EFFECTIVE OCTOBER 1
OpenRouter announced this morning that DeepSeek-V4 Pro moves to volume pricing on October 1: accounts above 500M tokens a month get roughly 30% off the current list price on both input and output, applied automatically, no prepay or commit required. Current vs. announced ($/M in / out):

  Tier                       Today            From October 1
  List (under 500M/mo)       $1.10 / $4.40    $1.10 / $4.40
  Volume (500M–5B/mo)        —                $0.77 / $3.08   (-30%)
  Volume (over 5B/mo)        —                $0.70 / $2.80   (-36%)

This is the largest single cut on a top-tier model this quarter, and it lands on a model family a lot of production extraction pipelines already run on. If you are modelling Q4 inference spend on DeepSeek-V4 Pro at today's rates, re-run it. Details: https://modelwatch.dev/pricing/openrouter-deepseek-v4-pro

2. MARLIN-70B (OPEN, APACHE 2.0) FROM WHITECAP RESEARCH
A second strong open 70B in a month. Whitecap's Marlin-70B trades a little extraction accuracy against Ferrite-70B for a noticeably better reasoning score:

  Model               Composite   Extraction   Tool use   Reasoning   $/M out (hosted)
  Marlin-70B (open)      80.3        92.6        94.2       76.0       $1.75 (Kestrel)
  Ferrite-70B (open)     78.9        94.1        95.0       68.2       $1.70 (Argent)
  Quillon-L              78.4        89.1        91.2       77.6       $4.50
  Sable-3.1 Mini         76.0        88.7        91.0       72.4       $0.44

Hosted on Kestrel today; Argent and Nimbus "shortly." https://modelwatch.dev/models/marlin-70b

3. AGENT EVALUATION HARNESSES: A ROUNDUP
Five harnesses for scoring multi-step agent runs, compared on what they replay, what they score, and what they cost to run:

  Harness          Replays tool calls?   Scores per step?   Cost tracking?   License
  Stepwise            yes                  yes                yes             Apache 2.0
  Larkspur Bench      yes                  yes                yes             Apache 2.0
  Brindle Scorer      yes                  no                 yes             commercial
  OpenTrace           yes                  no                 no              MIT
  Harnessline         no                   yes                no              commercial

Stepwise and Larkspur Bench are the two we would start with; both now read the shared replay-log format. Full notes: https://modelwatch.dev/roundups/agent-harnesses

